  const newStr = trimmed.replace(/[^A-Za-z0-9_-]/g, '`');

  return newStr;
}
```

For production use, test against WAF logs first — some systems block `Escaped` characters by default, and some ignore them entirely. The best approach is to strip out the payload structure itself rather than relying on the obfuscation to hide the payload.
